			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Extract Keybinding, Label, and Themes routers from monolithic dispatch\n\nReplace the inline match arms for `keybinding:*`, `label:*`, and `themes:*` commands in `DispatchMatch.rs` with dedicated router modules, following the established pattern already used by `HistoryRouter`. Each new module (`Keybinding/Router.rs`, `Label/LabelRouter.rs`, `Themes/Router.rs`) owns its command-to-handler mapping, routes through the existing UI/Navigation atoms, and returns `Option<Result<Value, String>>` for safe fallthrough.\n\nAlso relay four `tests.*` notification channels through `RelayToSky` in the gRPC service dispatcher, forwarding test lifecycle events (controller_created, run_started, run_ended, result) to the Sky webview via the `sky://tests/*` URI scheme.\n\nThe monolithic `DispatchMatch.rs` match block shrinks by ~50 lines and each command namespace now lives alongside its own module declaration in `mod.rs`, making future additions self-contained without touching the central dispatch chain.",
			"SHA": "f2eedba61768946d226f4440756c218af722cd04"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T23:17:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1867,
				17
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add NativeBus for direct Rust handling of swallowed IPC methods\n\nIntroduce Source/Shim/NativeBus.rs — a dispatch layer that handles IPC methods intercepted by SwallowMap natively in Rust, bypassing the Cocoon gRPC round-trip entirely. Covers file I/O (`tokio::fs`), terminal PTY, search, dialogs, status bar, and telemetry discard.\n\nWiring changes: DispatchMatch.rs now calls NativeBus::handle for Mountain-targeted methods instead of returning a bare Null ack, and the Shim module entry point registers NativeBus as a public submodule. Scattered formatting cleanup across InvokeProvider, Gate, SwallowMap, and several IPC handlers strips single-line wrapping from straightforward method bodies to match project PascalCase conventions.\n\nThe NativeBus table documents the routed prefix-to-handler mapping, with unimplemented search and dialog handlers returning stub ack responses for future native integration.",
			"SHA": "d1bbaa5a4aee20b182143bfd59060f9b463afbe4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T22:34:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1866,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Document Shim tiers and architecture in Arch.md\n\nAdd a new Shim Compatibility section to Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md covering both tiers of the deep-shim interception system:\n\n- **Low-Level Shim** (🟠, TierShim=Own|Preempt): Engine prototype hooks for Error, Emitter, Cancel, Dispose, Async, Timing interception.\n- **Coverage Shim** (🔵, TierShim=Proxy|Replace): Service-level routing for IPC SwallowMap, DI proxy, and AuditLog.\n\nAlso links to the Shim documentation and notes the Source/Shim/ Rust module location. This completes the documentation coverage for the interception layer introduced across the last five commits on the Current branch.",
			"SHA": "e4e3956cf47b55f13c8e072726535c21e3ca7160"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T22:26:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1866,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Wire Shim interception into both IPC dispatch paths\n\nInsert the Shim layer at two entry points so swallowed methods are\nintercepted before reaching any domain handler:\n\n- **DispatchMatch.rs** — Shim pre-check in `mountain_ipc_invoke` reads\n  `Gate::is_enabled()` and `SwallowMap::should_swallow()` to decide\n  whether to return a Null ack (Mountain/None targets) or passthrough.\n\n- **CreateEffectForRequest/Shim.rs** — New domain module that gets first\n  crack at every gRPC method via `Try!(Shim)` in the dispatch chain,\n  placed before all other domain handlers. Returns a Null-ack effect for\n  swallowed methods or `None` to fall through.\n\nAlso clean up the remaining AI-internal annotations from the initial\nShim implementation: remove the 🟠🔵 color/tier table and the\n`.hermes/microsoft/` doc reference from `Shim/mod.rs`, drop \"Land\"\nqualifier from `SwallowMap.rs`, and deduplicate the repeated subsystem\nfeature declarations in `Cargo.toml`.\n\nThe interception layer is fully gated behind `TierShim` (default: `None`)\nand compiles to zero overhead via dead-code elimination.",
			"SHA": "8e7ff15b9ef23c3c0a63203a1086dc97e0300645"
		},
